(TIM-41 - a time property can be read straight out of a format slot, and
 the `:02` zero-pad specifier applies to it, whether the time is stored in
 a name or read inline. The value is clock-dependent, but its width is
 not: a zero-padded hour is two characters whatever the clock says, which
 is how this stays a fixed-output probe.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-41.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the padded hour is two characters
   the padded minute is two characters
   an inline current time pads in a slot too
)
Get current time into now.
a text called 'the padded hour' is "{now's hour:02}".
a text called 'the padded minute' is "{now's minute:02}".
a text called 'the inline hour' is "{current time's hour:02}".
a buffer called 'the hour bytes' is "{'the padded hour'}".
a buffer called 'the minute bytes' is "{'the padded minute'}".
a buffer called 'the inline bytes' is "{'the inline hour'}".
If 'the hour bytes''s length is 2 then, print "the padded hour is two characters".
Otherwise, print "the padded hour is {'the hour bytes''s length} characters".
If 'the minute bytes''s length is 2 then, print "the padded minute is two characters".
Otherwise, print "the padded minute is {'the minute bytes''s length} characters".
If 'the inline bytes''s length is 2 then, print "an inline current time pads in a slot too".
Otherwise, print "the inline padded hour is {'the inline bytes''s length} characters".
